id: pm-yqe0mo
title: "Unknown-option recovery names three of six commands that accept the flag, capped silently and in arbitrary order, so the hint excludes the right answer while reading as exhaustive"
description: "pm deps --add reports '--add is a valid option on: comments, notes, learnings' while files, docs and test also accept it; findOtherCommandsForFlag slices to 3 with no truncation marker and no relevance ranking, and error-guidance renders it as a closed set ('if you meant one of those'). Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched unknown-option/recovery/cross-command/flag-suggestion items across all statuses; pm-8nyc (closed) built this feature, pm-gdi7 covers same-command flag suggestions, pm-cha95z covers diagnostic budget in aggregate. No open item covers the cross-command enumeration being silently partial."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli",diagnostics,error-contract,recovery-bundle
created_at: "2026-07-26T05:40:48.321Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T19:16:38.638Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-10T19:16:38.134Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-10T19:16:38.134Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "The cross-command candidate list is relevance-ranked before any cap is applied, so a binding cap retains the best candidates rather than the first-enumerated ones; when the cap binds, both the rendered prose and the structured recovery bundle declare truncation using this repository's existing truncation vocabulary; the structured bundle carries the full candidate set under its own bounded ceiling independent of what fits the prose sentence; a regression test asserts that --add on a non-accepting command enumerates files, docs and test among candidates or declares truncation; the closed-world phrasing 'if you meant one of those' is only emitted when the set is genuinely complete"
goal: project management = context management
objective: A recovery hint never asserts a closed candidate set it did not compute
value: Agents that trust structured recovery output stop being steered away from the correct command; one retry cycle saved per occurrence
why_now: "Reproduced live on the shipped 2026.7.26 build while probing the annotation family; the hint dropped pm files --add, which was the command actually needed"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: completed
expected_result: "Cross-command recovery ranks the complete candidate set, exposes bounded structured candidates with truncation receipts, and never presents a partial prose list as exhaustive."
actual_result: "Unknown-option recovery now returns the complete deterministic six-command fixture with exact total and explicit non-truncation, while bounded prose remains truthful and final CLI projection preserves the structured receipt."
